Subject: [PATCH] msm: mdss: Z500KL: keep the overlay ioctls

This MDSS turns away MSMFB_OVERLAY_*, MSMFB_BUFFER_SYNC and MSMFB_DISPLAY_COMMIT
unless the target is MDP3, because newer composers use MSMFB_ATOMIC_COMMIT. The
composer of this ROM, hwcomposer.msm8952 from display-caf, is HWC1 and uses the
old ones, so every frame failed with "Unsupported ioctl" and the screen stayed
on the boot logo. The code behind these ioctls is all still here: only the check
stops it.
---
--- drivers/video/fbdev/msm/mdss_fb.c
+++ drivers/video/fbdev/msm/mdss_fb.c
@@ -5182,7 +5182,7 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
-#ifdef TARGET_HW_MDSS_MDP3
+#if defined(TARGET_HW_MDSS_MDP3) || defined(CONFIG_MACH_ASUS_Z500KL)
 static bool check_not_supported_ioctl(u32 cmd)
 {
 	return false;
